# install.sh regenerates AGENTS.md (generic-agent mirror of CLAUDE.md) on every run — generated artifact, not tracked.
# Anchored to repo root so it does NOT also ignore nested files like plugin/commands/agents.md
# (git matches case-insensitively on macOS, so an unanchored rule swallowed the plugin command).
/AGENTS.md
# gen-plugin.sh output — generated build artifact, not tracked
dist/
# Local strategy artifacts under the otherwise-tracked research/ dir — keep off the public repo (cf. plans/, projects/)
research/2026-07-agent-audit.md
research/2026-07-portfolio-audit.md
research/2026-07-frontier-hunt-v2/
# Third-party agent skills installed via `npx skills add` (neondatabase/agent-skills, 2026-08-24).
# Kept LOCAL and usable, deliberately NOT tracked: CAST counts its own skills with
# `git ls-files 'skills/*'` (scripts/cast-stats-lib.sh:42), so committing these would silently move
# the count 18 -> 20 and fail stats-guard — and they are third-party content in a portfolio repo.
# Paths are root-anchored for the same reason as /AGENTS.md above (macOS matches case-insensitively,
# so an unanchored rule would also swallow nested paths like plugin/skills/neon).
# Adopting any of them properly is its own unit: regenerate cast-stats.json + README sentinels first.
.agents/
skills-lock.json
/skills/neon
/skills/neon-postgres
